  "decision_conditions": [
    "The loss of front garden area to be replaced with hardstanding to facilitate off street car parking would cause harm to the character and appearance of Meadway Conservation Area by means of the loss of traditional front garden area contrary to Core Strategy Policies CP30 and CP31, Development Management Document Policies DMD37 and DMD44 as well as having regard to Meadway Conservation Area Character Appraisal.",
    "The proposed development, in the absence of an adequate Arboricultural Impact Assessment and Arboricultural Method Statement, has failed to demonstrate that the proposal would retain and protect trees (protected by falling within Meadway Conservation Area) of visual amenity and biodiversity value within the site and surrounding area, contrary to Policies CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), DMD37 and DMD80 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014), G7 of the London Plan (2021), the National Planning Policy Framework 2021 as a whole and the British Standard for Trees in relation to design, demolition and construction (BS 5837:2012).\r\r"
